{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.pn_symmetric_groups_with_like_nucleons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.pn_symmetric_groups_with_like_nucleons","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L144-L151","doc":"**The symmetric `pn` channel sits with the like-nucleon pairs, not with the\ndeuteron.** A non-obvious consequence: `pn` splits, with its `I=1` component\nweighted like `pp`/`nn` and only its `I=0` component free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.only_singlet_channel_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.only_singlet_channel_free","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L134-L142","doc":"Only the `I=0` (deuteron) channel retains freedom — the `A`/`H` mix. So the\nselection rule leaves exactly **one** open parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.like_nucleon_forced_to_altT1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.like_nucleon_forced_to_altT1","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L127-L132","doc":"The like-nucleon channels are forced onto `T₁`, which carries **no residual\nfreedom** (its normalised weights are `0` on same-color pairs and `1/6` on each\ndifferent-color pair). So the `I=1` sector of `W` is fully determined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.charge_symmetric_pp_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.charge_symmetric_pp_nn","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L120-L125","doc":"**`W` is charge-symmetric between `pp` and `nn`** — the falsifiable\nconsequence. Both are `I=1`, so the interface coupling assigns them the *same*\ncolor system; the weight tensor cannot distinguish them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.trivially_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.trivially_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L102-L116","doc":"**The conjecture class is trivially inhabited** — the retraction, machine-\nverified rather than asserted.\n\n`⟨select, rfl⟩` witnesses it. So the four theorems below are not \"conditional on\nan open mathematical hypothesis\"; they are conditional on a *physical\nidentification*, and as mathematics they are `rfl` on a two-line table.\n\nDeliberately a `theorem` about `Nonempty`, **not** an `instance`: registering an\ninstance would let typeclass resolution discharge `[InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry]`\nautomatically and silently turn every conditional consequence below into an\nunconditional theorem about `select` — true, worthless, and easily misread as the\nphysics having been proved. Stating inhabitation as a `Nonempty` fact records it\nwithout changing what anything downstream depends on. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:isospin-selection-class-inhabited","label":"rem:isospin-selection-class-inhabited","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/isospin-selection-class-inhabited.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry.antisymmetry_forces_select","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry.antisymmetry_forces_select","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The exchange-antisymmetry constraint: the coupling is the selection rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry.coupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry.coupling","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The interface's induced color system for each nucleon-pair channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry.mk","kind":"ctor","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.InterfaceExchangeAntisymmetry","kind":"class","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L82-L100","doc":"**CONJECTURE (§3b-cond, no instance).** The two-nucleon interface carries\ndefinite antisymmetry under simultaneous exchange of color-sheet and flavor\nlabels — the hypothesis the selection rule rests on.\n\n**Corrected 2026-08-09.** This docstring used to end \"so it is not vacuously\nsatisfiable\". That is **false**, and `trivially_inhabited` below exhibits the\none-line witness `⟨select, rfl⟩`. The class fixes its own field to a definition\nalready in scope, so as a *mathematical* object it constrains nothing.\n\nWhat is genuinely open is the physics, and the distinction matters: the class\ndoes not assert \"some coupling satisfies this\"; it asserts \"the coupling the\n**physical** interface induces is `select`\". No Lean instance can establish\nthat, and none is registered, so every consequence below remains conditional —\njust not for the reason previously given. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.select","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.select","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L76-L80","doc":"**The selection rule.** Exchange-symmetric flavor (`I=1`) pairs with the\nantisymmetric color summand and vice versa — the only two couplings with overall\nexchange antisymmetry. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:nucleon-pair-isospin-channel","label":"def:nucleon-pair-isospin-channel","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/nucleon-pair-isospin-channel.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprColorSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprColorSystem","kind":"instance","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprColorSystem.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprColorSystem.repr","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instDecidableEqColorSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instDecidableEqColorSystem","kind":"instance","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.ColorSystem.symAH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.ColorSystem.symAH","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.ColorSystem.altT1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.ColorSystem.altT1","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.ColorSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.ColorSystem","kind":"inductive","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L69-L74","doc":"The two admissible color systems: `Alt² = T₁` (for `I=1`) and\n`Sym² = A ⊕ H` (for `I=0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.isospin_pair_dims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.isospin_pair_dims","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L64-L65","doc":"**The flavor pair space decomposes as `3 + 1 = 2 × 2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.isospinSummandDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.isospinSummandDims","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L61-L62","doc":"Dimensions of the isospin summands of `I=½ ⊗ I=½`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.isospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.isospin","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L56-L59","doc":"Total isospin of each channel: the triplet `I=1` is exchange-symmetric, the\nsinglet `I=0` exchange-antisymmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprNucleonPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprNucleonPair","kind":"instance","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprNucleonPair.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instReprNucleonPair.repr","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instDecidableEqNucleonPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.instDecidableEqNucleonPair","kind":"instance","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.pnAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.pnAlt","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.pnSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.pnSym","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.nn","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair.pp","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.NucleonPair","kind":"inductive","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ColorFlavorIsospinSelection.lean#L51-L54","doc":"The four nucleon-pair channels. ","signatureChunk":0}]}